  "caption": "Quinn's calendar was back-to-back meetings, and by mid-afternoon a zing shot from bum to calf. Sitting made it worse; standing helped a little.\n\nSciatica is radiating leg pain, usually from an irritated nerve root in the lower back, and most people improve with conservative care. Long sitting often stirs it up, and scan bulges are common even in people without pain.\n\nWhat can help: 1–2 minute walking breaks every 30 minutes, finding the movement direction that eases your leg, regular walks, and graded hip and trunk strength as it settles. Review it if it's not improving by 4–6 weeks.\n\nGet it checked promptly if you notice saddle numbness, bladder or bowel changes, worsening leg weakness, or symptoms in both legs.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
